                <pb facs="0512" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/858: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-11T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                                1928—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>404. Your 864, December 8, 5 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>Paragraph 2. Particulars of tariff schedules not necessary but information
                        concerning attitude of other governments and any steps contemplated or taken
                        by them are desired.</item>
                    <item>Paragraph 4. Noted and approved.</item>
                </list>
                <p>It is assumed that Commercial Attaché will give Department of Commerce complete
                    information.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
